       "PROJECT_FICHE_SHORT_TITLE": "Valle andaluz del hidrógeno verde electrolyser - Huelva",
       "PROJECT_FULL_TITLE": "Valle andaluz del hidrógeno verde electrolyser - Huelva",
       "COUNTRY_CONCERNED": "ES",
       "TECHNICAL_DESCR": "<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The <i>Andalusian Green Hydrogen Valley - Huelva</i> is Moeve’s strategic initiative to deploy 1,000 MW of electrolysis capacity in southern Spain, next to its Energy Parks in Huelva. Since 2022, the project has advanced significantly, supported by key industrial agreements.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">In Huelva, renewable hydrogen will decarbonise the transport sector through the production of biofuels, SAF — where Moeve held 38% of the Spanish market in 2024 — and hydrogen derivatives for maritime fuels, as well as meeting internal demand at the Energy Park. Hydrogen injection into the gas grid is also being assessed to support other industrial users.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The 1,000 MW planned in Huelva will be developed in phases: • <strong>Phase 1:</strong> 400 MW – COD 2028 (ONUBA, e‑ammonia) • <strong>Phase 2:</strong> 200 MW – COD 2030 (THARSIS, e‑methanol and eSAF) • <strong>Phase 3:</strong> 400 MW – COD 2030 (under development) The FID for ONUBA is expected in Q1 2026.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The Final Investment Decision (FID) for 300 MW of ONUBA Subproject was taken is scheduled for Q1in February 2026, which may lead to adjustments in the planned dates.</p>",
       "IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS": 3,
       "PROMOTERS": "Moeve S.A. (previously known as Cepsa) (ES) ",
       "COMMISSIONING_DATE": "12/2030",
       "CEF_ACTIONS": "9.15.4-es-s-m-24-hyandalusia-studiesi",
       "CEF_ACTION_FICHES": "https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/projects-details/43251567/101223699/CEF2027",
       "PCI_ID": 1414,
       "IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS_DESCR": "Permitting",
       "PCI_LIST_ACTIVE": 1,
       "STUDIES_OR_WORKS": "Studies",
       "NATURE_CODE": "PCI"
