       "CORRIDOR_NUMBER": 21,
       "PROJECT_FICHE_SHORT_TITLE": "Valdo Eume electrolyser",
       "PROJECT_FULL_TITLE": "Valdo Eume electrolyser",
       "COUNTRY_CONCERNED": "ES",
       "TECHNICAL_DESCR": "<p style=\"text-align:justify;\">Reganosa and Forestal del Atlántico, part of the Gadisa Group, are promoting the ValdoEume hydrogen valley initiative, which includes a first phase of 177 MW with a production of up to 27,000 t/y of RFNBO hydrogen with two electrolysis plants located in the municipalities of Mugardos (Triskelion facility with 77 MW) and As Pontes (H2Pole facility with 100 MW) connected by a 36 km hydrogen pipeline.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">&nbsp;In the next stages of implementation, ValdoEume will be able to expand to a total electrolysis capacity of up to 500 MW to produce 75,000 t/y of renewable hydrogen in 2035.</p><p style=\"text-align:justify;\">The renewable hydrogen generated in the valley will be used for e-methanol production (as Forestal del Atlántico currently imports this raw material), mobility, and injection into the new H2Med hydrogen network via the Coruña-Zamora pipeline. This will help to consolidate a major energy hub in the northwest of the Iberian Peninsula and reinforce Spain’s position as a strategic node for renewable hydrogen in Europe.</p>",
