       "PROJECT_FICHE_SHORT_TITLE": "Catalina electrolyser",
       "PROJECT_FULL_TITLE": "Catalina electrolyser ",
       "COUNTRY_CONCERNED": "ES",
       "TECHNICAL_DESCR": "<p>The Catalina project will deploy a 500 MW electrolyser integrated with approximately 1.1 GW of dedicated renewable generation (onshore wind and solar PV). This configuration will enable the production of around 48,000 tons per year of green hydrogen during the first decade of operation. The project also envisions a future expansion to reach up to 2 GW of electrolyser capacity.</p><p>&nbsp;Catalina has secured grid connection for export (~130 MW) and for import (~200 MW), reinforcing its integration with the national electricity system.</p><p>&nbsp;Located in Aragón, Spain, the project aims to establish a hydrogen industrial hub in the Andorra region, fostering the development of complementary industries as hydrogen offtakers and creating a significant positive impact on employment in this rural area.</p><p>The electrolyser will be connected via a 40 km dedicated hydrogen pipeline to the Spanish Hydrogen Backbone (PCI 9.1.3), ensuring sufficient capacity to transport hydrogen produced by the plant at its ultimate scale of up to 2 GW.</p>",
       "IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS": 3,
       "PROMOTERS": "CI ETF I Renato Ptx Holdco, S.L.U.  (ES)",
