       "PROJECT_FULL_TITLE": "ErasmoPower2X electrolyser",
       "COUNTRY_CONCERNED": "ES",
       "TECHNICAL_DESCR": "<p>ErasmoPower2X is an innovative green hydrogen and e-methanol project development in Saceruela, Ciudad Real, Spain, aligned with Spanish and EU climate and energy goals. It will produce up to 80,000 tons of green hydrogen annually, supported by a 650 MW electrolysis plant, 1.2 GW solar photovoltaic installation, 890 MW of wind PPAs, and opportunity to use an integrated battery to improve the business case. Integrated into the national hydrogen backbone, developed by Enagás Infraestructuras and located at &lt;1km from the plants location, it decarbonizes steel and petro-chemical industries, stimulates economic growth, security of supply of energy and reindustrialisation.</p><p>The project will connect with the Spanish H2 Med Backbone, which is part of the European H2 backbone.</p>",
